{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/skill-layout/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Skills directory at repo root\nAll skills SHALL live in `skills/` at the Darkfactory repo root (`~/.darkfactory/skills/`), not in `.claude/skills/`.\n\n#### Scenario: skills/ directory exists with correct structure\n- **WHEN** a developer clones the Darkfactory repo\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/skills/` exists and contains exactly 12 subdirectories: `mission`, `grill`, `language`, `prd`, `adversarial`, `dispatch`, `tdd`, `test-quality`, `security`, `mission-resume`, `mission-status`, `mission-init`\n- **AND** each subdirectory contains a `SKILL.md` file with valid frontmatter (name, description, user-invokable fields)\n\n### Requirement: Legacy .claude/skills/ removed\nThe `.claude/skills/` directory inside the Darkfactory repo SHALL be deleted.\n\n#### Scenario: No .claude/skills/ in repo\n- **WHEN** the migration is complete\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/.claude/skills/` does not exist\n- **AND** `git ls-files .claude/skills/` returns no output\n\n### Requirement: .codex/skills/ duplicates removed\nThe `.codex/skills/` directory inside the Darkfactory repo SHALL be deleted.\n\n#### Scenario: No .codex/skills/ in repo\n- **WHEN** the migration is complete\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/.codex/skills/` does not exist\n- **AND** `git ls-files .codex/skills/` returns no output\n\n### Requirement: Forked skills present and self-contained\nSix externally-sourced skills SHALL be forked into the repo as owned files, not symlinks.\n\n#### Scenario: grill skill forked from grill-me\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/grill/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `grill`\n- **AND** the skill content matches the behavior of the original `grill-me` skill\n\n#### Scenario: prd skill forked from write-a-prd\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/prd/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `prd`\n\n#### Scenario: language skill forked from ubiquitous-language\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/language/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `language`\n\n#### Scenario: tdd skill forked with companion files\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/tdd/`\n- **THEN** `SKILL.md` exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** all 5 companion files exist: `deep-modules.md`, `interface-design.md`, `mocking.md`, `refactoring.md`, `tests.md`\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `tdd`\n\n#### Scenario: test-quality skill forked from test-quality-review\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `test-quality`\n- **AND** the skill content matches the behavior of the original `test-quality-review` skill (except the frontmatter name field)\n\n#### Scenario: security skill forked from security-review\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/security/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists and is a regular file (not a symlink)\n- **AND** the frontmatter name is `security`\n- **AND** the skill contains no references to toyo-review or toyo-specific review sections\n\n### Requirement: Mission-family skills moved to skills/\nThree existing skills SHALL be moved to `skills/`. Two are moved unchanged; one is renamed.\n\n#### Scenario: mission-resume skill moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-resume`\n- **AND** the skill content is identical to the original `.claude/skills/mission-resume/SKILL.md`\n\n#### Scenario: mission-status skill moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-status/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-status`\n\n#### Scenario: mission-init skill renamed from darkfactory-init\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the file exists with frontmatter name `mission-init`\n\n### Requirement: Mission skill preserved with updated references\nThe existing mission SKILL.md and its companion files SHALL be moved to `skills/mission/`.\n\n#### Scenario: mission skill and companions moved\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/mission/`\n- **THEN** `SKILL.md` exists\n- **AND** `templates/` subdirectory exists with all original template files\n- **AND** `prompts/` subdirectory exists with all original prompt files\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7G9G103078A9GV0CH477WG","ts":"2026-04-27T12:58:51Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/setup-verification/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init skill replaces /darkfactory-init with symlink verification\nThe `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md` skill SHALL check that `install.sh` has been run by verifying symlinks exist, instead of checking two separate source locations.\n\n#### Scenario: Symlink check replaces dual-location check\n- **WHEN** `/init` runs its skill checks\n- **THEN** it verifies that `~/.claude/skills/<name>` is a symlink pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each of the 12 owned skills\n- **AND** it does not check `.claude/skills/` inside the repo or `~/.darkfactory-skills/` as alternate install locations\n\n#### Scenario: Broken symlink detected and reported\n- **WHEN** a skill symlink exists in `~/.claude/skills/` but does not resolve (dangling symlink)\n- **THEN** `/init` reports it as broken with the expected target path\n- **AND** it suggests running `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` to fix it\n\n#### Scenario: Missing symlink detected and reported\n- **WHEN** a skill is not symlinked (symlink absent entirely)\n- **THEN** `/init` reports it as missing\n- **AND** it suggests running `~/.darkfactory/install.sh`\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init reports all 12 expected skills\nThe skill SHALL check for all 12 skills by their current names.\n\n#### Scenario: Skill list is correct\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` checks skills\n- **THEN** the checklist includes: `mission`, `grill`, `language`, `prd`, `adversarial`, `dispatch`, `tdd`, `test-quality`, `security`, `mission-resume`, `mission-status`, `mission-init`\n- **AND** the checklist does NOT include: `grill-me`, `write-a-prd`, `ubiquitous-language`, `darkfactory-init`, `test-quality-review`\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init still verifies CLI tools\nThe skill SHALL still check for required CLI tools as before.\n\n#### Scenario: CLI tools checked\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs\n- **THEN** it checks for `codex`, `darkfactory-dispatch`, `gh`, `openspec`, and `jq`\n- **AND** for each, it reports whether it is installed and authenticated (where applicable)\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init reports install instructions when setup is incomplete\nIf any symlinks are missing, the skill SHALL print a single command to fix everything.\n\n#### Scenario: Install command shown on failure\n- **WHEN** one or more skill symlinks are missing or broken\n- **THEN** `/mission-init` prints: `Run: ~/.darkfactory/install.sh`\n- **AND** it exits after showing the report (does not attempt to create symlinks itself)\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init verifies coverage tool per detected language\nThe skill SHALL detect the project language from build files and check the appropriate coverage tool is installed.\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for Rust project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `Cargo.toml` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks whether `cargo-tarpaulin` is installed\n- **AND** reports `[x] cargo-tarpaulin` if installed, or `[ ] cargo-tarpaulin (install: cargo install cargo-tarpaulin)` if not\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for TypeScript/Node project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `package.json` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks `package.json` `dependencies` and `devDependencies` for `c8`, `@jest/coverage`, `istanbul`, or `jest`\n- **AND** reports the found package (e.g. `[x] jest (built-in coverage)`) or `[ ] no coverage package found (install: npm install -D c8)` if none found\n\n#### Scenario: Coverage tool checked for Python project\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` at the root\n- **THEN** it checks whether `pytest-cov` is installed\n- **AND** reports `[x] pytest-cov` if installed, or `[ ] pytest-cov (install: pip install pytest-cov)` if not\n\n#### Scenario: No recognized language detected\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory with no `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, or `requirements.txt` at the root\n- **THEN** it reports \"No recognized language detected -- coverage tool check skipped\"\n\n### Requirement: /mission-init still initializes OpenSpec if not initialized\nThe skill SHALL still run `openspec init` if `openspec/config.yaml` does not exist in the current directory.\n\n#### Scenario: OpenSpec init on first run\n- **WHEN** `/mission-init` runs in a directory without `openspec/config.yaml`\n- **THEN** it runs `openspec init --tools claude,codex --force`\n- **AND** it reports \"OpenSpec: initialized\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
